  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Verdinexor and Beta-lactamase (KPC-2) through a multi-step pathway. Verdinexor is predicted to target DNA-directed RNA polymerase subunit beta, which in turn is a target of H3B-8800 and Bromotheophylline. Both H3B-8800 and Bromotheophylline are known to inhibit Beta-lactamase (KPC-2), indicating that Verdinexor may exert its effect through a similar mechanism. The high scores in both paths suggest a strong predictive relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Verdinexor influences Beta-lactamase remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role of DNA-directed RNA polymerase subunit beta as a mediator in the interaction between Verdinexor and Beta-lactamase, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm this hypothesis.",
